  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Light, expressive purple-white",
    "overview": "The user approved a new purple-white visual world and its centered opening with a community board on 2026-11-10, then instructed that it be applied. White space, artistic display type, gentle purple gradients and floating white cards give discovery and sharing an expressive, readable home. After trying the background, the user explicitly selected the original soft mist rather than the stronger ribbon variation, then clarified that the mist should flow on both sides with a white center.\n\nThis is the current visual specification, with an explicit implementation boundary: the new world is implemented on the homepage; other functional pages retain their existing IAVSE foundation until they are migrated deliberately. Homepage tokens are implemented by [the landing stylesheet](src/app/iavse-landing.css) and [landing components](src/components/landing/IavseLanding.tsx). Tokens prefixed `legacy-` document the existing functional-page foundation in [iavse-system.css](src/app/iavse-system.css), [the scoped template input](src/styles/rbp-template.input.css) and [the host bridge](src/app/rbp-bridge.css). They are scoped implementation facts, not a second homepage direction. The [homepage brief](.impeccable/surfaces/src-components-homeproductshowcase-tsx.md) owns its composition.\n\nThe earlier application baseline retains its [RBP Portfolio source attribution](docs/portfolio-frontend.md), pinned at `1581b9b8e5876f60e5eb844970747506980c4412`. The new homepage and its analytic background are independently authored public website code; they do not revive the cancelled Cloudlight migration or incorporate private Pro materials. [PRODUCT.md](PRODUCT.md) owns business, permission and license boundaries. Authored blog themes, canvas documents, uploaded images and third-party previews keep their own appearance and rights.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A white homepage with purple actions, deep plum text, soft mist on both sides and a white center.",
      "Artistic licensed display and wordmark faces paired with readable Geist body text.",
      "Transparent, uncolored navigation with the original brand at left and real account state at right.",
      "White floating content cards, fine-pointer response and bounded viewport entry.",
      "Explicit legacy scope for functional pages pending gradual migration.",
      "Truthful public content, labeled examples and accessible motion fallbacks."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Transparent Header Rule",
        "body": "Keep the homepage header uncolored and transparent, without a frosted layer; its white appearance comes from the page below it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Source Identity Rule",
        "body": "Keep source previews and authored work recognizable and attributed. A template fallback must remain visibly labeled as a fictional example.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Hierarchy Rule",
        "body": "Verify Chinese, English and Japanese wrapping at the actual viewport width; keep body copy and compact metadata distinct from artistic headings.",
        "section": "typography"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the purple-white homepage tokens within the new homepage and keep legacy functional-page scope explicit.",
      "Do keep the homepage header transparent, uncolored and free of backdrop blur.",
      "Do preserve the user-selected soft mist on both sides, white center, top clearance and gentle pointer response.",
      "Do verify Chinese, English and Japanese hierarchy and wrapping on desktop and mobile.",
      "Do reveal content once over 650ms with 24px travel and cap 70ms staggering at 210ms; reveal keyboard-focused content immediately.",
      "Do retain real public content, meaningful empty states, labeled fictional examples and motion fallbacks."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't describe the whole site or either complete dual-UI version as already migrated.",
      "Don't replace the accepted mist with a mandatory high-contrast ribbon or rolling-band standard.",
      "Don't apply the platform skin or entry animation inside authored work or third-party previews.",
      "Don't invent users, posts, endorsements or engagement totals to fill a layout.",
      "Don't import private Pro materials, revive the cancelled direct Cloudlight migration or expand any license.",
      "Don't claim authorship of Geist, Cormorant Garamond or ZCOOL XiaoWei; retain attribution and their existing licenses."
    ]
  }
